# Cloudflare Pages serves index.html with status 200 for every unknown
# path when the publish root has no 404.html. 404.html is that switch.
# Do not add "/* /index.html 200". That rule would bring the homepage back
# for missing files, including these discovery URLs.
#
# Pretty URLs: Pages already serves /list from list.html, and a request for
# /list.html is a 308 back to /list. Do NOT add `/list /list.html 200`.
# That rewrite fights the pretty URL and loops forever
# (308 Location: /list, and the same loop on /list.html).
# The same trap is `/something/* /something.html 200`. It drops the splat
# and lands on /something. Do not re-add either rule.
#
# These targets are .md or .json, not .html, so pretty URLs do not rewrite
# them back onto the source path. They are not the /list loop.
# Keep them above the splat rule. A splat is slower, and it must not sit
# above a rule it could shadow.
/agent-submit  /agent-submit.md   200
/agent-onboard /agent-onboard.md  200
/public/.well-known/agent-onboard.json  /.well-known/agent-onboard.json  301
#
# Profile pages use the query string, which pretty URLs leave alone:
#   /agent?id=<id>  serves agent.html
# Old /agent/<id> links redirect once, then stop.
/agent/*       /agent?id=:splat   301
